  "preamble": "Loss of the glottal fricative [h] is among the most common consonant deletions. Word-initial h- disappeared from Latin already in the Classical period (hence its silence in all Romance languages), from Greek during the Koine period (psilosis), from most Mongolic languages after Proto-Mongolic, and from presyllables in several Chamic languages.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Elision, Consonant Loss",
